# All Classes — Full QA Mandatory (ABSOLUTE — NEVER ASK)

**The owner has said this repeatedly. Do not make them say it again.**

## Mandate (non-negotiable)

Every shipped Bible class (**Bruiser, Archer, Lancer, Mage, Cleric**, and every future class) must reach **Knight-bar depth**:

- `docs/<CLASS>_QA_GATE.md` — full matrix, meta-critic contract, three tiers
- **Per-factory-row scenario** (`tests/skills/<id>_scenario.gd` / `tests/passives/<id>_scenario.gd`)
- **Tier 1** `run_<class>_qa_gate.ps1` — **PASS**
- **Tier 2 live** `run_<class>_live_qa.ps1` — **PASS**
- Movement planning smoke for every movement skill (or dedicated scenario that proves the same commit path — **no silent skips**)
- Matrix rows promoted toward **`PASS`** (not left at `HARNESS_ONLY` while claiming done)

Class kits are **drafts** (`.cursor/rules/skill-lists-are-drafts.mdc`). Run thorough automated QA for work you touch. Do **not** recite owner sign-off / LOCK in replies.

## Forbidden (instant rule violation)

| Do | Why forbidden |
|----|----------------|
| Ask "want me to run Lancer live?" / "should I expand Archer matrix?" | Owner already answered: **yes, all classes, full depth** |
| Stop when one class gate is green while others are shallow or untested | Task is **all classes**, not one gate |
| Report "gates pass" and end turn with `HARNESS_ONLY` matrix / skipped movement smoke | Headless green ≠ class complete |
| Remove skills from movement smoke "because complex" without replacing with per-skill planning proof | Coverage hole; fix the harness or add scenario |
| Offer optional follow-ups instead of continuing | **Continue until blocked by a real error**, then fix and re-run |

## Required agent behavior

1. **Work the full class list** each session until time/context hard-stops — do not close a turn on a single-class win.
2. **Run both gates** (Tier 1 + Tier 2 live) for **every** class touched or claimed complete.
3. **Fix failures in a loop** — re-run the failing suite after each fix; do not hand-wave.
4. **Changelog** must list **per-class** gate result (PASS/FAIL) and matrix counts when class files change.
5. **No permission gate** for "expand QA" or "run live suite" — only code edits that change gameplay need `interpret-plan-permission.mdc`.

## Session exit criteria (all must be true or document FAIL blockers)

- [ ] `run_bruiser_qa_gate.ps1` + `run_bruiser_live_qa.ps1` — PASS
- [ ] `run_archer_qa_gate.ps1` + `run_archer_live_qa.ps1` — PASS
- [ ] `run_lancer_qa_gate.ps1` + `run_lancer_live_qa.ps1` — PASS
- [ ] `run_mage_qa_gate.ps1` + `run_mage_live_qa.ps1` — PASS
- [ ] `run_cleric_qa_gate.ps1` + `run_cleric_live_qa.ps1` — PASS (upgrade gate doc if still stub)
- [ ] `run_planning_qa_gate.ps1` — PASS when planning/combat paths touched

If any row is FAIL: **fix or report exact `[FAIL]` lines** — never imply the task is done.

